# Scrye dogfood self-scan — triaged Trivy exceptions.
#
# The CI "image" job scans Scrye's own image with Trivy and gates on FIXABLE
# HIGH/CRITICAL findings (`--ignore-unfixed --severity HIGH,CRITICAL`). Per
# CLAUDE.md § Dependency hygiene, all fixable findings must be resolved; only
# genuinely unfixable upstream/OS-level items may remain and are documented in
# the README.
#
# This file is the allowlist for any *fixable* finding that cannot be resolved
# immediately (e.g. a fix exists upstream but is not yet in the pinned base
# image). Each entry MUST carry a dated justification comment. Keep it empty
# unless an exception is genuinely required — an unexplained id here defeats the
# purpose of the gate.
#
# Format: one vulnerability id per line, e.g.
#   CVE-2024-12345  # 2026-07-03: fixed upstream in libfoo 1.2.3, awaiting base image bump
#
# (No exceptions at authoring time — the pinned base image and scanner versions
#  were chosen to be free of fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings.)
